course: dictionary
lesson: 15410
title: Spree: doing a lot at once
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A spree is a short time when you do a lot of something you enjoy, without holding back. Read the words around it to find the meaning. «Zara went on a shopping spree and bought five pairs of shoes.» Five pairs in one go tells you she bought a lot, all in a short burst.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning in place of the word: «Zara went on a short burst of buying and bought five pairs of shoes.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Spree can also be used with spending money. «Ben went on a spending spree and spent all his birthday money in one afternoon.» Spending spree tells you he spent fast, so his savings were gone quickly. In the news, a spree of crimes means many crimes one after another.
fact: A spree is a short time when you do a lot of something without holding back.
fact: A shopping spree means buying lots of things in one short burst.
fact: A spending spree can empty your savings fast.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad goes on a spree of buying motor cars and crashing them.
fact: A spree of crimes means many crimes one after another, as in a news report.
exercise: «Zara went on a shopping spree and bought five pairs of shoes.» What is a shopping spree? | A long walk to the shops | *A short burst of buying lots of things | A sale where everything is free | A list of things to buy
exercise: «The police said there had been a spree of burglaries in the village.» What does a spree of burglaries mean? | A new kind of lock | A party for the police | One burglary on a quiet day | *Many burglaries one after another
exercise: «Toad went on a spree of buying motor cars and crashing them.» What does spree suggest? | A tidy list of rules | Sitting quietly in a car | *Doing lots of one wild thing without holding back | A slow walk around a garden
test: «After a birthday spree at the sweet shop, Maya had no pocket money left.» What is the spree? | A birthday cake with candles | *Lots of buying in one short burst | A quiet walk home with her friends | A rule about sweets
test: «The cat had a spree of mischief and knocked over three plants.» What does spree of mischief suggest? | *Lots of naughty things done one after another | Cats do not like plants | Good behaviour all day long | One quiet nap in the sun
exam: Which is a good way to check the meaning of spree? | Look only at the title of the book | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Skip the sentence and never think about it again | Count the letters in the word
